{"title":"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 38","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Mean_Inequality_Chain)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Mean Inequality Chain)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Calculus_Optimization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Calculus Optimization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is inscribed in a semicircle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> so that its base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> coincides with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. \nPoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> does not coincide with either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bddba95aecf34b8003cb54e3994210becea740a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=AC+BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />. Then, for all permissible positions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7abd61302b03e3849cdac7cd85151be865e29a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ s^2\\le8r^2\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ s^2=8r^2 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ s^2 \\ge 8r^2 \\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ s^2\\le4r^2 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ s^2=4r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"364\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a872b645d046a8eed82e49f40459e85e0dc9a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((-50,0)--(-30,40)--(50,0)--(-50,0)); draw(Arc((0,0),50,0,180)); draw(rightanglemark((-50,0),(-30,40),(50,0),200)); dot((-50,0)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(-50,0),SW); dot((-30,40)); label(&quot;C&quot;,(-30,40),NW); dot((50,0)); label(&quot;B&quot;,(50,0),SE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"128\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bddba95aecf34b8003cb54e3994210becea740a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=AC+BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/0340bebd8e780970fcbcb055a08b6ecddf022c2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2 = AC^2 + 2 \\cdot AC \\cdot BC + BC^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"247\" height=\"16\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is inscribed and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is the diameter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is a right triangle, and by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d718ec799528b31a7d960d95d791bdb8fe88a07a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC^2 + BC^2 = AC^2 = (2r)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"19\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1c30b5ae976b8d12a2542930e4da519d0dcce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2 = 4r^2 + 2 \\cdot AC \\cdot BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"179\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a74d02689bf5a22779c054b79a2e04ee920677f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AC \\cdot BC}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"39\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4ce68f89804d625cac175b5189eefcda4083a9bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot [ABC] = AC \\cdot BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" />.  That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29d3648c6afe0738d100f85a056e7a1423fa8650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2 = 4r^2 + 4 \\cdot [ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" />.  The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> can also be calculated by using base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  The maximum possible value of the altitude is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so the maximum area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e2221c84f16a3f75ae07e5023384cc40d9c05357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9af83ed42dcb11742426b97766fb6b601e651e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2 \\le 8r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Mean_Inequality_Chain.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Mean_Inequality_Chain)\">Solution 2 (Mean Inequality Chain)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Mean Inequality Chain)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/822e35cd4a9074a4e2620bbd7ff3eb756948f2db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=2r$\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79ed539b440dcc1813f0406de80c468646c7747e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC^2+BC^2=4r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>By quickly considering extreme cases (when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> coincides with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />) we can suspect that the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is achieved when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the origin of the semicircle. We will prove this using the Mean Inequality Chain. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e496e01efa8d9bfe5d0f9f8ac59e8b120a5e81f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=x, BC=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/a/c1ab190cc3a630395c6bd3b7bcd8526fef8ffb57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=4r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />. By QM-AM, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/567499ea4020fc05916cc1f7ca9973a5ea48b27b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{x^2+y^2}{2}}\\ge \\frac{x+y}{2}=0.5s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"207\" height=\"45\" />. Plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/a/c1ab190cc3a630395c6bd3b7bcd8526fef8ffb57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=4r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/4/794a531813b2dcd5d725a69b5b99fe583c9f0005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{2}r\\ge s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"22\" />. Square both sides, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" /> is correct.\n</p><p>~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Calculus_Optimization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Calculus_Optimization)\">Solution 3 (Calculus Optimization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Calculus Optimization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution utilizes optimization techniques taught in Calculus 1 classes.\n</p><p>Let the equation of the semicircle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/caba62b9f731685229020dd0ae74b586ef30dcd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=r^2, y\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" />. Notice that in this semicircle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/1/c41f8d450f2795e9c9edd5e9f622c345c252802c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sqrt{r^2-x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f0f160a9a0a34e0253d36435e1899a284ca5948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(x, \\sqrt{r^2-x^2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"23\" />. Using the Pythagorean Theorem with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a84b5f2db734de1fe08be38996c485f6650fd9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A (-r,0), B(r,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />, finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, differentiating and finding the absolute maximum, we can find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" /> is correct. \n</p><p>P.S.: The process of bash is omitted here since anybody that actually learned optimization problems and paid attention to it (this is core curriculum in regular college math) should be able to bash it out.\n</p><p>~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/ind